-- The Hunting Grounds (the book's Area 2 map, 6A-6J), redrawn in our pieces. Turned half round from
-- the book's page so the stairs up from the gift shop come in on the west, and condensed from the
-- book's 13 x 14 octagon to the mat: wider and a little flatter, the octagon and its cut corners
-- kept. The studies (with the stairs up between them) stand in the middle as a block with its
-- doorway, the World of Tomorrow and the lecture theatre along the east side with their doors;
-- each of those has a board of its own. Every exhibit sits where the book has it: the cave model
-- and the razorbark tree north, the kitchen in its corner, the jungle by the stairs, the jars by
-- the studies, the skull, the model city and the big bird along the south. The south wall is left
-- off: the DM's side.

