spots:
-- key  | x,y   | name                      | line
6A      | 14,11 | the giant skull           | The armoured skull of a burrowing beast breaks up through the floor. It's hollow inside.
6B      | 13,13 | the model city            | A model city twenty feet long, its towers taller than a person, tiny trains whirring through it.
6C      | 6,12  | the big yellow bird       | A stuffed flightless bird as big as a horse, chewing on stuffed greens. Something stands very still behind it.
6D      | 2,9   | the spiky sketch          | An artist's drawing of an enormous wingless beast covered in spikes.
6E      | 8,6   | the pickling jars         | Two jars of yellow-green brine, each holding something like a brain with a beak.
6F      | 6,9   | the jungle                | Ten feet of dense jungle you can't see through. Humid, and full of distant birdsong.
6G      | 3,5   | the misted cabinet        | A glass case fogged over from inside. Something grows in there. Break it and it spreads.
6H      | 6,3   | the razorbark tree        | A tree reaching right up to the ceiling. Its bark is worth money to the right buyer.
6I      | 11,4  | the cave model            | A model cave system with six peep holes. Through one, a skeletal hand wearing a gleaming ring.
6J      | 15,4  | the little kitchen        | A whole working kitchen: knives, pots and polished cupboard doors you can see reflections in.
stairs  | 5,7   | the top of the stairs     | Where the stairs from the gift shop come up. The hall ahead is full of exhibits, and it feels like being watched.
